
  <sn><md>### Basic Structure of a Data Declaration in C

A **declaration** in C tells the compiler: **What is the data type, what is the name, and how the variable should behave?**

Simplest Variable Declaration

```c
data_type identifier;
```

Example:

```c
int age;
```

| Part  | Meaning                    |
| ----- | -------------------------- |
| `int` | Data type                  |
| `age` | Identifier (variable name) |
| `;`   | Ends the declaration       |

**Structure**

```text
┌───────────┬────────────┬─────────┐
│ Data Type │ Identifier │    ;    │
└───────────┴────────────┴─────────┘
     int          age
```
